  "conclusion": "A failure boundary was measured for 2 of 8 parameters (brightness first failed at 0.08; perspective first failed at 0.18). No failure was reached within the tested range for blur_sigma, noise_sigma, jpeg_quality, ambient, vignette, gamma; the per-frame photometric calibration makes global brightness, gamma and ambient offset largely irrelevant until contrast is destroyed. Blur mixes triangle interiors, noise perturbs the per-cell threshold, JPEG creates block artefacts, perspective stresses fiducial detection, and vignetting reduces corner contrast. These are SIMULATED observations, not physical camera results; the exact crossing points are in processed/summary.csv.",
